  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Jones, A polynomial invariant for knots via von Neumann algebras (Bull. AMS 12:1, 1985) — the original Jones polynomial paper, via the trace on a type II_1 factor and the braid group.\n\n**A polynomial invariant for knots via von Neumann algebras** — Vaughan F. R. Jones. Bulletin (New Series) of the American Mathematical Society, Volume 12, Number 1, January 1985.\n\nThe paper that introduced the Jones polynomial. Alexander's theorem represents any tame oriented link as the closure of a braid (b, n) with b in Bₙ; Jones constructs the invariant from a trace on the von Neumann algebra generated by the braid representation, with Markov moves controlling well-definedness.\n\n**Why it may bear here.** This corpus *is* built on the Markov trace on H_n(q): `J_L(q) = tr_M(ρ(β_L))` is the Hecke-Skein convention in AGENTS.md §7a, and this is where that construction comes from. Registering the origin paper, not claiming a specific result from it is in use.",
      "lang": "en",
